question/id #uuid "9977a1dd-4a81-52ff-bede-89adf3e6a78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-19037" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}})≈{11.49}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19037/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "32c95188-10a9-5114-99b0-cb90db5d77b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "72673e86-c085-5291-8bec-166da72a0e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "73d308c4-816e-53bb-9c5e-3a09bfaddfb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "84cd7a4c-ec32-59ce-a7d2-70ca0fd02759" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection/e7b7ed4c0eee3932aefbd621bbd4ad75ee4b3803b6786b241b5151651dffe901" :answer/id #uuid "d2487dac-0617-58ae-8a51-f5bdcd054680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f26f37a-46b8-5fce-81b3-84be685ab68e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77159/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-77159/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-77159/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" "q-77159/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-77159/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-77159/selection/e7b7ed4c0eee3932aefbd621bbd4ad75ee4b3803b6786b241b5151651dffe901"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77159" :question/id #uuid "09283c16-ce85-51a9-9e26-ee1e56005470" :question/math-academy-id "q-77159" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,4,1),$ $Q(3,4,2)$ and $R(3,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P,$ $Q$ and $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,q=⟨3,4,2⟩,\\,r=⟨3,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨3,3,1⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection/92a13d6deea6ea42c4bbcad26e1d95f5a4d1723746fb3fde87982ea9cfc5c5a5" :answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection/271d337a1e562bb54bb9379eb174c33646ecf35161383f3fd1e8d44aeb78b3bc" :answer/id #uuid "eb1e08c5-8191-51cb-828c-4e1bf4d18edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection/ade074deb6f4e5d6e8883fcad6ed460296204f1821a5aa552f4867b6984b7ed8" :answer/id #uuid "a8481d0e-1847-5899-a263-24206ff622f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{91}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection/d1e3edc3840f96397f6a6625a4a90a9671648d7e5ee86467f2a83b43b8823623" :answer/id #uuid "f68369eb-d5b2-597a-8ad3-4e02ef54893c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection/6b096eb12f5b015a9021b7451b71cce3e2ca1f97c7cc58fc665b184758ff7293" :answer/id #uuid "c48d61db-8a7b-58a9-baa3-b45f0e2b2e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{77}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4237779a-fb1d-5aae-9935-ca22c819fe5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101511/selection/92a13d6deea6ea42c4bbcad26e1d95f5a4d1723746fb3fde87982ea9cfc5c5a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-101511/selection/92a13d6deea6ea42c4bbcad26e1d95f5a4d1723746fb3fde87982ea9cfc5c5a5" "q-101511/selection/271d337a1e562bb54bb9379eb174c33646ecf35161383f3fd1e8d44aeb78b3bc" "q-101511/selection/ade074deb6f4e5d6e8883fcad6ed460296204f1821a5aa552f4867b6984b7ed8" "q-101511/selection/d1e3edc3840f96397f6a6625a4a90a9671648d7e5ee86467f2a83b43b8823623" "q-101511/selection/6b096eb12f5b015a9021b7451b71cce3e2ca1f97c7cc58fc665b184758ff7293"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101511" :question/id #uuid "16a09fd3-be95-51b4-b0ac-0c24039ae9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-101511" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,1)$, $B(3,1,-2)$, and $C(-1,1,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,1,-2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}})≈{86}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101511/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101511"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection/9065e450684baa8e61df08be51d6ad4312af70399bfb3dc0e200b2a0d7963b7b" :answer/id #uuid "48b4dd83-fc3a-5279-9506-b1c1c610adae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection/71d45aef1091987f4823341c5762c02fee20af7a997ca678a0c1ef53cd49f5ea" :answer/id #uuid "6ea035f0-6207-54f9-8514-fc252b0a6a65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection/0fe39b4e66699b1a7eb1c40a28632d17621e5f1ef17a4bafdcd47fac82b383c8" :answer/id #uuid "16104c2f-285a-58e3-a912-1c5c32735793" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection/2b66031fbecba2d4885f17a2c6ac30af285e4f8340b721a11d5436e29a67fe2f" :answer/id #uuid "d7796c45-683b-5992-8c9f-34c50eb36c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection/4a5cefad56819447672d3f14e74e4b47d99ae691906a5dcf7a0171eae8f040dd" :answer/id #uuid "551cfa18-cedc-5bbe-8306-3487d020644c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0865b498-b4a5-5b7f-ba31-8063a63b2589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19107/selection/2b66031fbecba2d4885f17a2c6ac30af285e4f8340b721a11d5436e29a67fe2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-19107/selection/9065e450684baa8e61df08be51d6ad4312af70399bfb3dc0e200b2a0d7963b7b" "q-19107/selection/71d45aef1091987f4823341c5762c02fee20af7a997ca678a0c1ef53cd49f5ea" "q-19107/selection/0fe39b4e66699b1a7eb1c40a28632d17621e5f1ef17a4bafdcd47fac82b383c8" "q-19107/selection/2b66031fbecba2d4885f17a2c6ac30af285e4f8340b721a11d5436e29a67fe2f" "q-19107/selection/4a5cefad56819447672d3f14e74e4b47d99ae691906a5dcf7a0171eae8f040dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19107" :question/id #uuid "26ec9194-f492-518e-8975-e0a3b197c76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19107" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19107/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection/fdad1f8a9ae245b85e8d5bf8256ba7cc36a81d54412ee184a99721006622ab47" :answer/id #uuid "7cf1043e-f893-5baa-9db6-4c2fb8c3639b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection/8054304fddf4b48693ad35887faf99224ec7548e30e7afaf6bf777ee8da45450" :answer/id #uuid "b8f831b4-cf64-570c-b2d2-906e374febed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" :answer/id #uuid "d9fd197d-e501-5e43-8c1c-2232a6ef539c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "1f9ac76d-964b-5482-9d58-9e89c6296713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "27bcfe70-6989-5359-9ab8-99a8be1e27c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdaea567-3b0b-54de-9b16-a108031e4eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101510/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" :answer-field/choices ["q-101510/selection/fdad1f8a9ae245b85e8d5bf8256ba7cc36a81d54412ee184a99721006622ab47" "q-101510/selection/8054304fddf4b48693ad35887faf99224ec7548e30e7afaf6bf777ee8da45450" "q-101510/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" "q-101510/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-101510/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101510" :question/id #uuid "af00a80e-1320-5335-a947-5ce3ede8cf57" :question/math-academy-id "q-101510" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(-4,3,1)$, $Q(-1,2,0)$, and $R(-10,5,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨-4,3,1⟩,\\,q=⟨-1,2,0⟩,\\,r=⟨-10,5,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨-4,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨-10,5,3⟩-⟨-4,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-6)+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-22}{\\sqrt{11}\\cdot \\sqrt{44}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)={180}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101510/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101510"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection/40004f3a9f80cd2b8c8ced451398a2416045f3013cb2c3e70dc308927d2a692b" :answer/id #uuid "d0f223ca-0fea-5bae-8cdd-b11ad4571b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{27}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "853ea703-1d96-539c-87e3-e34d3d095438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection/b7fe8e75c2bc57bbd5b52f5b86c6d83bad893a77467b8d445d5318a899a4e770" :answer/id #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection/b84d516698a1be204527297a088cf90216a400178e15b5cece027ef82c083708" :answer/id #uuid "9a09a8bd-4160-5cba-b8e6-8131c8959abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection/71d45aef1091987f4823341c5762c02fee20af7a997ca678a0c1ef53cd49f5ea" :answer/id #uuid "12fb3ba3-823c-5cfc-b083-6ce78c505fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4556650-d240-5520-9d69-8f8ef1163437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69831/selection/b7fe8e75c2bc57bbd5b52f5b86c6d83bad893a77467b8d445d5318a899a4e770" :answer-field/choices ["q-69831/selection/40004f3a9f80cd2b8c8ced451398a2416045f3013cb2c3e70dc308927d2a692b" "q-69831/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" "q-69831/selection/b7fe8e75c2bc57bbd5b52f5b86c6d83bad893a77467b8d445d5318a899a4e770" "q-69831/selection/b84d516698a1be204527297a088cf90216a400178e15b5cece027ef82c083708" "q-69831/selection/71d45aef1091987f4823341c5762c02fee20af7a997ca678a0c1ef53cd49f5ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69831" :question/id #uuid "e553e89a-b69b-5299-b9b3-9573916538d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-69831" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,1,2)$, $Q(1,3,2)$, and $R(4,5,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,1,2⟩,\\,q=⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,r=⟨4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,3,2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨4,5,-2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-69831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection/de586a1dd17063ac90cdcd39140ca79458bd7d0ef833914d36f0d2c62ed0f086" :answer/id #uuid "18fbf17f-6676-5ef4-94f3-f5c84e4ee533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{84.7}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection/2772a2c6649d78b62a999a25b5e5441dace69e1d278525ac821c32900d964246" :answer/id #uuid "004c9eb0-5a71-5df8-b041-27504f9d73ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{110.8}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection/04093c17714b559524bce599bac316788805d89c9762af952bec54f3200d4901" :answer/id #uuid "ed774057-02be-5493-896f-c9b973d6a63c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{132.4}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection/a31de5bf9346ab6a161f598253e4be493bd5b84956ff87c33975d1a89a592fa7" :answer/id #uuid "3644af28-f706-5f0f-9ae0-d5fc607f96c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{104.5}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection/48ca68791bd1671e980148222f0292098d818d96187453aeb1f9998a8841bf48" :answer/id #uuid "b1c9fdee-1a62-5d99-b8a6-6f15b43fb29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{92.3}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbb7ddab-cbbf-5ec3-9438-35e2697ee7d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19038/selection/a31de5bf9346ab6a161f598253e4be493bd5b84956ff87c33975d1a89a592fa7" :answer-field/choices ["q-19038/selection/de586a1dd17063ac90cdcd39140ca79458bd7d0ef833914d36f0d2c62ed0f086" "q-19038/selection/2772a2c6649d78b62a999a25b5e5441dace69e1d278525ac821c32900d964246" "q-19038/selection/04093c17714b559524bce599bac316788805d89c9762af952bec54f3200d4901" "q-19038/selection/a31de5bf9346ab6a161f598253e4be493bd5b84956ff87c33975d1a89a592fa7" "q-19038/selection/48ca68791bd1671e980148222f0292098d818d96187453aeb1f9998a8841bf48"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19038" :question/id #uuid "ba4d9a12-1a1e-55c8-94d8-119632f1d338" :question/math-academy-id "q-19038" :question/problem "Given that $p\\cdot q=-5$, find the angle between $p=⟨4t,-2,t⟩$ and $q=⟨1,3,-3⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $p\\cdot q=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =-5 \\\\ 4t\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 3+t\\cdot (-3) & =-5 \\\\ 4t-6-3t & =-5 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨4(1),-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{21}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTHerefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}})≈{104.5}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection/5925bef74d9593b1a517c264a2c49ec5b06eb1da01b8b814c5455bf64faa0c2d" :answer/id #uuid "a4eef7ee-ce27-568c-aa25-74f1486ec107" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection/271d337a1e562bb54bb9379eb174c33646ecf35161383f3fd1e8d44aeb78b3bc" :answer/id #uuid "4ee2a05a-ca70-5223-ba9e-36cd6fa08e55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection/5483c6ac22b1784c48819fb7438d7c5d56c7e573394aec3adef5166d5b5958b0" :answer/id #uuid "6eaac85c-277b-51f1-baf6-a4d8434347b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection/e7b7ed4c0eee3932aefbd621bbd4ad75ee4b3803b6786b241b5151651dffe901" :answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection/1c85b9398507c77816c62bf033d97e288d87ddf33dd00345c153510ecc9b9978" :answer/id #uuid "cb9d024a-612a-5b88-b561-2eca5dd12c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89db74db-3d63-59f5-b41d-544e3f33dabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77164/selection/e7b7ed4c0eee3932aefbd621bbd4ad75ee4b3803b6786b241b5151651dffe901" :answer-field/choices ["q-77164/selection/5925bef74d9593b1a517c264a2c49ec5b06eb1da01b8b814c5455bf64faa0c2d" "q-77164/selection/271d337a1e562bb54bb9379eb174c33646ecf35161383f3fd1e8d44aeb78b3bc" "q-77164/selection/5483c6ac22b1784c48819fb7438d7c5d56c7e573394aec3adef5166d5b5958b0" "q-77164/selection/e7b7ed4c0eee3932aefbd621bbd4ad75ee4b3803b6786b241b5151651dffe901" "q-77164/selection/1c85b9398507c77816c62bf033d97e288d87ddf33dd00345c153510ecc9b9978"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77164" :question/id #uuid "61191758-28d5-55a6-95f0-ed679272a908" :question/math-academy-id "q-77164" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77164/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection/d999c5a03b6934563ccbbde8be7d324e9403c79fd9121aa429cd1046db4cc7c7" :answer/id #uuid "00c34ec0-c0f2-5eaa-bd8f-92c1fa6ac6de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120.9}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection/10ce793e6a4db9d70573b20f6616acd3d6d03adddaf439c31ebf2b7efee9006d" :answer/id #uuid "28b8bdbb-40f0-5e9c-9af6-75ad034239f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{116.6}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection/a03b1d2246d763d8968f24cf853e980dfed0dabec24b322b78788bb849b7f645" :answer/id #uuid "047be692-7ec1-5921-9e3e-a096d5ab0960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{113.8}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection/3926e90df7bef3ae3f91d9d76c8b3731fd01a4053ceb8f9b14f6508005fa23eb" :answer/id #uuid "8c46e53c-d1ff-5dc9-ad5b-7d8ca4d94a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{111.1}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection/97f612d170f15b6c3d7cac7e6c9ffac27a9c9188c8512be445880c4ba792767f" :answer/id #uuid "23bbb5d2-e5e3-5cee-9ce1-e977f27b0c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{122.3}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f467919b-d9c3-556d-b9c6-eb60fabcc3ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101514/selection/10ce793e6a4db9d70573b20f6616acd3d6d03adddaf439c31ebf2b7efee9006d" :answer-field/choices ["q-101514/selection/d999c5a03b6934563ccbbde8be7d324e9403c79fd9121aa429cd1046db4cc7c7" "q-101514/selection/10ce793e6a4db9d70573b20f6616acd3d6d03adddaf439c31ebf2b7efee9006d" "q-101514/selection/a03b1d2246d763d8968f24cf853e980dfed0dabec24b322b78788bb849b7f645" "q-101514/selection/3926e90df7bef3ae3f91d9d76c8b3731fd01a4053ceb8f9b14f6508005fa23eb" "q-101514/selection/97f612d170f15b6c3d7cac7e6c9ffac27a9c9188c8512be445880c4ba792767f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101514" :question/id #uuid "852d0fcb-212d-5f7f-bb3f-afcaa190e7c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-101514" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-10$, find the angle between $a=⟨-4t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨2,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-10$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-10 \\\\ (-4t)\\cdot 2+3t\\cdot 1 & =-10 \\\\ -8t+3t & =-10 \\\\ -5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-4(2),\\,3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{10\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{116.6}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101514/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101514"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection/5ac0407d35b447e38f1c6b44cafbf4f7296825a5593094385504dfaa4f8260f0" :answer/id #uuid "fb6a7436-5d40-5ead-afe9-8fc3f33b83ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{70.99}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection/33d7aa17169ca5d40bd93b283857ddf7fb1a421ec119248f13e9320a4c5fff62" :answer/id #uuid "33d889d7-3053-5698-b65c-fe5ae9aa07f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75.22}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection/66d6024fee8037a9ea505d1be21e2402d72303ef184f9ca4dc126a8414e2faec" :answer/id #uuid "08336714-fd00-56fc-9883-ef766d26fd89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{85.33}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection/365e228474bda208f1ade1c7be3a3004696d4321a951c76e75f2a8c9325608e4" :answer/id #uuid "bf85c120-7483-5553-bdcd-a44069470789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{78.55}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection/d0592abd902a2d28b09e2ccac47d20523610d5d27eb4922edaa41e827693c5ef" :answer/id #uuid "7934f66e-abaa-5481-ab13-a79e21a04132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{80.44}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69c601c3-8547-5f8b-8af3-b0698702489b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101520/selection/d0592abd902a2d28b09e2ccac47d20523610d5d27eb4922edaa41e827693c5ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-101520/selection/5ac0407d35b447e38f1c6b44cafbf4f7296825a5593094385504dfaa4f8260f0" "q-101520/selection/33d7aa17169ca5d40bd93b283857ddf7fb1a421ec119248f13e9320a4c5fff62" "q-101520/selection/66d6024fee8037a9ea505d1be21e2402d72303ef184f9ca4dc126a8414e2faec" "q-101520/selection/365e228474bda208f1ade1c7be3a3004696d4321a951c76e75f2a8c9325608e4" "q-101520/selection/d0592abd902a2d28b09e2ccac47d20523610d5d27eb4922edaa41e827693c5ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101520" :question/id #uuid "8fc7cf1b-c116-59a4-83f2-94ca1412ae63" :question/math-academy-id "q-101520" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(t,5,3)$, $E({t}^{2},2,t)$ and $F(t+3,{t}^{2},1).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩,\\,e=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩,\\,f=⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3,\\,t-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,{t}^{2}-5,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =6 \\\\ ({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot ({t}^{2}-5)+(t-3)\\cdot (-2) & =6 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3t-3{t}^{2}+15-2t+6 & =6 \\\\ -5t+21 & =6 \\\\ -5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨{3}^{2}-3,-3,3-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨3,{3}^{2}-5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}})≈{80.44}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-101520/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101520"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection/cc859611013ae39fba086ac280ae5f345eb23311294b7f5b86e2290ff3ec4734" :answer/id #uuid "f3aaf77e-f91e-5eec-80e8-ad79e8adb224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{59}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection/593d1db5fafc50613699d8e0aba83121d8bc911ba9abc7a6baa9377daf35f502" :answer/id #uuid "a3f9b012-c354-5d6e-9581-72bdf697d50f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{67}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection/1c85b9398507c77816c62bf033d97e288d87ddf33dd00345c153510ecc9b9978" :answer/id #uuid "7d53a02b-b33e-51dd-8ab2-e9af5a421db7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection/6c339bbbf680fd438fc4befc8d333c50832dd8fcaec7fc0032cffd699a749572" :answer/id #uuid "4d60903b-6a7a-53d2-83bb-a4aa0851a070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection/74621dff1232131b8826107e64da06bd3303b32c116231a9daa2ce9c400d4cf7" :answer/id #uuid "4a098196-3c16-5eab-ba4d-21e17c7dbf00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{62}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae427d9-2381-531f-87a7-c13fc1fb292e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125079/selection/593d1db5fafc50613699d8e0aba83121d8bc911ba9abc7a6baa9377daf35f502" :answer-field/choices ["q-125079/selection/cc859611013ae39fba086ac280ae5f345eb23311294b7f5b86e2290ff3ec4734" "q-125079/selection/593d1db5fafc50613699d8e0aba83121d8bc911ba9abc7a6baa9377daf35f502" "q-125079/selection/1c85b9398507c77816c62bf033d97e288d87ddf33dd00345c153510ecc9b9978" "q-125079/selection/6c339bbbf680fd438fc4befc8d333c50832dd8fcaec7fc0032cffd699a749572" "q-125079/selection/74621dff1232131b8826107e64da06bd3303b32c116231a9daa2ce9c400d4cf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125079" :question/id #uuid "1d872083-4e1c-5f3c-8347-aaf05eb74faf" :question/math-academy-id "q-125079" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(t,1,1)$, $B(3t,1,3)$ and $C(3,-2,{t}^{2}).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=4.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,1,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨3,\\,-2,\\,{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,1,\\,3⟩-⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,{t}^{2}⟩-⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-t,\\,-3,\\,{t}^{2}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =4 \\\\ 2t\\cdot (3-t)+0\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1) & =4 \\\\ 6t-2{t}^{2}+0+2{t}^{2}-2 & =4 \\\\ 6t-2 & =4 \\\\ 6t & =6 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,2⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨3-1,\\,3,\\,{1}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{26}})≈{67}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125079/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125079"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
